From e5ed1d56e1f8b50610563c0c3033afa1b25f1940 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:53:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Let a concurrency-cancelled run be superseded by a
 later green run of the same workflow

PR acceptance, no-required-check fallback, MERGED path. Live: example-project
PR #12 (head abcdef12) had a full green workflow run before merge, but an earlier
run of the same workflow (cancelled by the concurrency group when a label event
started the next run) left one `check ... infra cancelled` row, so kanban_complete
was refused and nothing after the merge could change that.

Why: the fallback keys runs by (name, app, check suite). The cancelled run and its
replacement are different workflow runs, hence different suites, so _unsuperseded
(same workflow run, higher run_attempt) never saw them as related.

Fix: after _unsuperseded, partition_at_merge drops a `cancelled` job only when
Actions identity proves a later green run (actions_runs: job -> check-run proof ->
actions/runs/{id}, validated for id, workflow_id, event, head SHA, timestamps):
same workflow_id, event and head SHA; a different, later-created workflow run that is
completed/success with updated_at at or before the merge; a same-named job in it that
started before and succeeded by the merge; exactly one job of that name per workflow
run on both sides (unreadable same-name jobs count as siblings). Everything else stays
fail closed: failure/timed_out/other conclusions, no later run, a later run that is not
success or concluded after the merge, non-Actions apps, 404s. The required-check path
and the OPEN path never read workflow runs. 7363e1a28a / 95e3d3cf35 behaviour is unchanged.

Proof: 53 new tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pr_cancelled_superseded.py), 4 red
on the old code, no existing assertion edited. 27 source mutants over the new
conditions, all killed after adding cases (redundant guards removed). 20 consumer
files: 566 passed. Read-only evaluation of the gate against PR #12 returns
success, with check run 123456789 no longer in the receipt.
